{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/475371-siphon-exploit-home-brew","id":475371,"title":"Siphon [Exploit home brew]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-09T22:10:36-07:00","id":475371,"title":"Siphon [Exploit home brew]","content":"First off before I detail and describe the 'what' I feel I should first explain the why. For the last few months on and off again I have been trying to find a way to make it possible for a demon's mortal lackeys to upkeep the levels of aether in their exploited gadgets if they ever reached a point where the demon simply did not have the time to do it himself. So far other than hiring another demon or using a form gadget of 'essence drain' and risking your minions on every use I have yet to find a way that would make sense. If you can think of a way to allow (non-demon blooded) mortals a way to transfer aether other I'm all ears but if not feedback on the following home-brewed exploit would be greatly appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Siphon (Exploit)</b><br /> Concept: After studying aetheric transfer a demon decided to try to find a way to remove some of the inefficiencies and enable the transfer from one 'container' directly to another instead of wasting aether with an unnecessary transfer to themselves. Built on how the machine would move it's own resources and the inbuilt system of aetheric transfer every demon has, this scholar of a demon developed the method he dubbed 'siphon'.<br /> Example perquisites: [to be decided]<br /> Dice pool: Wits + Occult + primum<br /> Action: Extended ( 1/roll = 1 minute [ or 5 minute?] )<br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> <u>Roll results</u><br /> DF: Instead of the careful and precise slow movement of aether from one container to another you manage to pull it all out at once and dump it into the air to dissipate. Roll for compromise (-1) or take a condition.<br /> F: No progress is made and the stop in movement makes the process harder, the next roll is made at -1.<br /> S: You may move a number of aether from one 'container' of aether to another. The amount you can move is up to the number of successes rolled to a maximum of the container's capacity.<br /> E: +3 aether can be moved on top of the amount for a standard success.<br /> *Note: It can only move aether from an existing 'container' to another. Examples include a demon, a stockpile and an exploited gadget. It can move aether to a container but not create a container (stockpile).<br /> <br /> <b>Final note(s)</b><br /> -The purpose of this is to be made into a gadget and enable 'safe' use by mortals.<br /> -I explored the possibility of making it an embed but to not make it better than default aether transfer methods I had to make it an extended action which broke rules for an embed.<br /> -I tried to make the actual exploit useful beyond just as a gadget but I admit I do not feel it quite stacks up at the moment, I am just unsure how to make it better without it being too much or over shadow the standard method too much.<br /> <br /> I thank any who reads this and provides opinions, feedback, criticism etc ahead of time. I do appreciate any outside opinions so I can form a stronger and more stable idea that is as balanced as possible when I show my St. I will be trying to research it in character but feel it is best that I at the least bring a rough draft for him to approve of before I try to begin the in character experimentation. (If they don't like it I'll keep it for my own game I'm running)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:15:57-07:00","id":475393,"title":"","content":"The effect you're looking for is essentially a near-field gadget based on Devour Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:25:33-07:00","id":475421,"title":"","content":"That is something I had not even considered hu. Ya that could be easier and I do feel this could be rather redundant potentially. I'll explore it as a possibility thank you satchel but if that falls through I may still fall back on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:31:34-07:00","id":475424,"title":"","content":"It honestly doesn't seem convenient. It would cost aether to use as an exploit and cost aether to use as just a given demon ability. Without the exp cost. So as an exploit its just underwhelming. <br /> <br /> For gadgets, wouldn't it still cost aether to use? Unless the gadget's sole purpose was to absorb aether. But then adding it to a gadget that has an embed or exploit would be a huge and dangerous task in the first place. For less exp and about the same effort there's a merit that provides aether everyday. <br /> I mean you could always find a beat trick with the essence drain form ability. <br /> <br /> Gadgets aren't really common in my games so I'm trying to figure out how id make it viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:54:15-07:00","id":475430,"title":"","content":"Gadget cost 1 aether per month to maintain but don't cost to activate, an exploited gadget can also act as a stockpile so it can store aether it gathers. <br /> <br /> I started with it as an embed and though 100x slower than the standard aether transfer I felt it more or less over shadowed the standard method as well as breaking the rules that all embeds are instant or reflexive as the balancing factor was it being an extended action and 5 minutes per roll. Efficient for aether at the cost of inefficient of time. More or less the exact mechanics of the exploit but no aether cost and risk of compromise on each roll (with a bonus to roll) with the exceptional success having no risk of compromise for that roll.<br /> <br /> Other point against the embed version being used for this intended gadget was the fact that because it is an embedded gadget it can no act as a stockpile so would need to wire the two 'containers' up and pump from what I'd assume was immobile to a more mobile stockpile all because it had no buffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}